<section id="specify">
<h2>When to specify Nevara</h2>
<p>The simple decision rule:</p>

<div class="rule-card">
<p><strong>Reach for Nevara when:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>The client is <strong>upgrading from in-stock or flat-pack cabinets</strong> and wants real plywood construction without a semi-custom budget</li>
  <li>A <strong>builder needs to hit a price point</strong> but wants WW Wood reliability, one portal, and a predictable ~5&ndash;6 week lead</li>
  <li>The design is <strong>white Shaker, frameless</strong> — and speed and consistency matter more than customization</li>
  <li>You're quoting against a home-center stock line and want to win on construction quality at a comparable number</li>
  <li>The project is volume work — rentals, spec homes, ADUs, multi-unit — where a repeatable single-SKU program is an advantage</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Reach for a different Pinnacle brand when:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>The finish or color is the design driver — <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/shiloh">Shiloh</a> (widest program) or <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/aspect">Aspect</a> (value framed, stains available)</li>
  <li>The client wants specialty frameless fronts — acrylic, HPL, TFL, PV, GOLA handleless — <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/eclipse">Eclipse</a> is the answer</li>
  <li>The design calls for inset or face-frame construction — <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/shiloh">Shiloh</a> or <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/aspect">Aspect</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

